<h1>📸 Physiological Sensor & Placement Image Gallery</h1>
<p>This single document contains embedded visuals and all the key links you need to review and choose images for your handbook. Click any link to open the full gallery in a browser.</p>

<!-- Section: Embedded Physiological Diagrams -->
<div class="section">
  <h2>🔬 Embedded Physiological Diagrams</h2>

  <h3>PPG (Photoplethysmography) Pulse Wave</h3>
  <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/Photoplethysmogram_%28PPG%29_pulse_wave.svg"
       alt="Photoplethysmography PPG pulse wave">
  <p>Typical PPG waveform showing the pulsatile blood volume signal. Useful for illustrating what the sensor *measures*. Source: Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 4.0).</p>

  <h3>Short PPG Signal Segment</h3>
  <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Short_photoplethysmogram_%28PPG%29_signal.svg"
       alt="Short PPG signal">
  <p>Short segment of a PPG signal showing individual heart beats. Good for explaining peak detection and HRV basics. Source: Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 4.0).</p>

  <h3>Biosignal Overlay: ECG, PPG, Respiration</h3>
  <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/Sample_Biosignals_%28ECG%2C_PPG%2C_RIP%29.svg"
       alt="Sample ECG PPG respiration signals">
  <p>Comparison of ECG, PPG, and respiration signals — helpful for explaining how modalities relate. Source: Wikimedia Commons.</p>

  <h3>PPG Fiducial Points</h3>
  <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0d/Photoplethysmogram_%28PPG%29_pulse_wave_fiducial_points.svg"
       alt="PPG fiducial points">
  <p>Annotated PPG waveform showing fiducial points. Useful for explaining feature extraction for HRV. Source: Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 4.0).</p>
</div>

